EMMS has several buffers/views, let me break it down:

**Main buffers:**
- `emms-playlist-mode` — the active playlist
- `emms-browser-mode` — library browser (artist/album/track tree)
- `emms-stream-mode` — radio streams

**Essential commands to know first:**
```
M-x emms              ; open playlist
M-x emms-browser      ; open browser
M-x emms-smart-browse ; opens both side by side
```

**Default navigation in playlist:**
```
n / p       next/previous track in playlist
SPC         pause/resume
s           stop
>           seek forward
<           seek backward
+/-         volume up/down
r           toggle repeat
z           toggle shuffle
```

**Browser navigation:**
```
RET         expand/collapse or add to playlist
E           expand all
C           collapse all
```

---

**Tag editing** — this is where it gets important. EMMS has `emms-tag-editor`. The workflow:

```
M-x emms-tag-editor-edit        ; edit tags of track at point
M-x emms-tag-editor-edit-marked ; edit multiple marked tracks
```

Inside the tag editor buffer:
```
C-c C-c     save and apply changes
C-c C-r     rename file based on tags
```

It uses a plain text buffer where you edit fields directly — similar feel to your org editing.

